# Cargo & agent-shell safety (craft)

## Why it looked "stuck"

Cargo was **not** compiling forever. Parallel agent shells queued on
`target/.cargo-lock` with **zero stdout** until the lock freed. That looks like
a hang but is a lock queue.

## Compile before test (required)

Always run **check first**, then test — never jump straight to `cargo test`:

```bash
./scripts/check-with-log.sh              # phase 1 only (~seconds, compile errors)
./scripts/test-with-log.sh               # check + test (script runs check automatically)
./scripts/test-with-log.sh -p craft-actor --test group_rebalance
```

`test-with-log.sh` runs `cargo check` automatically unless `CRAFT_SKIP_CHECK=1`.
If check fails, tests are skipped.

## One cargo at a time

- **Never** launch multiple `cargo` commands in parallel in the same workspace (including background Shell calls).
- Cargo holds an exclusive lock on `target/.cargo-lock`; extra invocations wait **silently** with no stdout.
- Before a new build/test, ensure no other cargo is running: `./scripts/cargo-status.sh`

## Use the logging wrappers

Prefer project scripts over raw `cargo test`:

```bash
./scripts/cargo-status.sh
./scripts/test-with-log.sh --workspace --all-features
./scripts/test-with-log.sh -p craft-actor --test group_rebalance
```

Progress is written to **`target/test-run.log`** with timestamps and `CARGO_LOG=cargo::core=info`.

## When output looks stuck

1. **Do not** spawn another `cargo` — it joins the lock queue and makes things worse.
2. **Read** `target/test-run.log` (tail) — output may arrive there before the agent terminal.
3. If lock persists >30s after aborting prior runs: `pkill -9 cargo rustc; rm -f target/.cargo-lock`
4. Re-run **one** `./scripts/test-with-log.sh …` command.

## Shell call discipline

- At most **one** active `cargo` Shell per workspace session.
- Do not chain diagnostic commands (`echo`, `python`, `rustc`) while cargo is still running.
- Full workspace gate: single `./scripts/test-with-log.sh --workspace --all-features` (allow several minutes); do not start a second until it finishes.
- Narrow first when iterating: `./scripts/test-with-log.sh -p <crate> …` before full workspace.

## Debug env vars

- `CRAFT_LOG_REBALANCE=1` — rebalance planner/executor lines on stderr (multi-Raft).
